static const char body_12_2[] =
    "1Electrolytic cells\n"
    "0Use electricity to force a\n"
    "0nonspontaneous reaction. The signs of\n"
    "0the electrodes flip: the anode is\n"
    "0positive and the cathode is negative,\n"
    "0but oxidation still happens at the\n"
    "0anode.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Uses\n"
    "0Electroplating, refining aluminum\n"
    "0from bauxite, splitting water into H2\n"
    "0and O2, recharging a battery.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Faraday's laws\n"
    "21 F = 96485 C/mol of electrons\n"
    "2Q = I*t   (coulombs)\n"
    "2moles of e- = I*t/96485\n"
    "0Then use the half reaction ratio to\n"
    "0get moles of product.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Linking to thermodynamics\n"
    "2dG = -n*F*E\n"
    "0n is moles of electrons transferred.\n"
    "0A positive E means a negative dG, so\n"
    "0spontaneous.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Nernst equation\n"
    "2E = E0 - (0.0592/n)*log(Q)  at 25 C\n"
    "0Cell potential falls as the reaction\n"
    "0proceeds and Q rises. At equilibrium\n"
    "0E = 0 and the battery is dead.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Relating E0 and K\n"
    "2log K = n*E0/0.0592\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Corrosion\n"
    "0Rusting is iron oxidized by oxygen.\n"
    "0Galvanizing coats steel with zinc,\n"
    "0which is more active and corrodes\n"
    "0first as a sacrificial anode.";

static const char body_12_3[] =
    "1Types of decay\n"
    "2alpha: emits He-4\n"
    "2  A drops by 4, Z drops by 2\n"
    "2beta minus: neutron -> proton + e-\n"
    "2  A unchanged, Z rises by 1\n"
    "2beta plus (positron)\n"
    "2  A unchanged, Z drops by 1\n"
    "2gamma: photon only\n"
    "2  A and Z unchanged\n"
    "2electron capture: p + e- -> n\n"
    "2  A unchanged, Z drops by 1\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Penetrating power\n"
    "2alpha: stopped by paper or skin\n"
    "2beta: stopped by thin aluminum\n"
    "2gamma: needs thick lead or concrete\n"
    "0Alpha is the least penetrating but\n"
    "0the most damaging if inhaled or\n"
    "0swallowed.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Balancing nuclear equations\n"
    "0The mass numbers must sum equally on\n"
    "0both sides, and so must the atomic\n"
    "0numbers. Use that to identify the\n"
    "0missing particle.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Half-life\n"
    "2N = N0*(1/2)^(t/t_half)\n"
    "0After n half-lives, (1/2)^n remains.\n"
    "0Half-life is unaffected by\n"
    "0temperature, pressure or chemical\n"
    "0form.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Band of stability\n"
    "0Light nuclei are stable near a 1:1\n"
    "0neutron to proton ratio; heavy ones\n"
    "0need about 1.5:1. Everything above\n"
    "0bismuth-83 is radioactive.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Fission and fusion\n"
    "0Fission splits a heavy nucleus,\n"
    "0releasing neutrons that can sustain a\n"
    "0chain reaction. Fusion joins light\n"
    "0nuclei and powers stars. Both convert\n"
    "0mass to energy by E = mc^2.\n"
    "0\n"
    "1Uses\n"
    "0Carbon-14 dating (5730 y), medical\n"
    "0tracers, radiation therapy, smoke\n"
    "0detectors (americium-241).";

